# Netlify. Pagefind bundles are read cross-origin by the shared search
# box: bondy.io, developer.bondy.io and lang.bondy.io each index only their
# own pages, and the box merges the three in the browser at query time. The
# dynamic import of pagefind.js and every index shard it then fetches are
# cross-origin requests, so without this header the other properties silently
# contribute no results.
#
# These are public static files on a public site, so * is the honest value —
# and _headers cannot echo an allow-list back per request anyway.
/pagefind/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
